WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:03.580
We have some bad hombres here and we're gonna
get 'em out.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:07.020
Well, that's it, the final debate of 2016
is over.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.440
And everyone's talking about the same things
we've heard time and again.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.340
Donald thinks belittling women makes him bigger.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.120
Why don't you give back the money that you've
taken from certain countries

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.360
that treat certain groups of people so horribly?

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:26.280
And Trump supposedly threatening the very
fabric of our democracy.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:30.500
That the loser concedes to the winner and
that the country comes together,

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.220
in part, for the good of the country,

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.360
are you saying
you're not prepared now to commit to that principle-

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.040
What I'm saying is that I will tell you at
the time.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.410
I'll keep you in suspense.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:42.410
Well, Chris, let me respond to that because
that's horrifying.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:47.350
And then in the last ten minutes of the final
debate of the presidential contest,

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:51.320
we finally talked about a little thing called the debt.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.740
But the non-partisan committee for responsible
federal budgets says that Secretary Clinton,

00:00:55.750 --> 00:01:01.750
under your plan debt would rise to 86% of
GDP over the next ten years.

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:08.590
Mr Trump under your plan they say it would
rise to 105% of GDP over the next ten years.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:13.840
Trump wants to cut taxes and raise spending
while denying that it would explode our debt.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.560
I say they're wrong because I'm going to create
tremendous jobs.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:21.060
And Clinton wants to raise spending and raise
taxes

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.560
while denying that would have any effect on job growth.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:29.620
We are going where the money is, we are going
to ask the wealthy and corporations

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.140
to pay their fair share.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:37.460
And there is no evidence whatsoever that that
will slow down or diminish our growth,

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.400
in fact I think just the opposite.

00:01:39.409 --> 00:01:42.869
Most economists accept that high thresholds
of government debt

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:45.589
correlates with low economic growth.

00:01:45.589 --> 00:01:47.949
But you didn't get to hear that perspective
in the debates,

00:01:47.949 --> 00:01:50.800
brought to you by our wonderful two party system.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:54.540
This debate is sponsored by the Commission
on Presidential Debates.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:58.860
So while everyone's talking about rigged elections,
leaked emails and puppets.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:02.700
No puppet, no puppet... you're the puppet.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.999
Remember that both candidates will run up
the debt, oppose free trade, deport more immigrants

00:02:06.999 --> 00:02:10.369
and likely mire us in endless middle eastern
conflicts.

00:02:10.369 --> 00:02:11.400
Happy Voting!

